 "result_text": "I changed the default to `dayfirst=False` in `parse()` in `delorean/interface.py`. With `dayfirst=True` and `yearfirst=True`, dateutil read `2017-05-02` as year, day, month, which is why you got February 5th.\n\nI couldn't run your exact example. `parse('2017-05-02T05:38:49.899Z')` fails in this environment with `AttributeError: 'zoneinfo.ZoneInfo' object has no attribute 'localize'`. That error comes from how `Delorean` handles the local timezone here, not from the date parsing. I didn't change it.\n\nI checked the fix two other ways:\n- `parse('2017-05-02 05:38:49')` now gives May 2nd.\n- dateutil's own parser, called with `dayfirst=False, yearfirst=True`, gives `2017-05-02 05:38:49.899000+00:00` for your string.\n\nI didn't run the test suite: pytest found no tests to run. Anyone who relied on the old day-first default will now need to pass `dayfirst=True` explicitly.",
